m9ajSSIhFm4kgrRjL6m8yrqArZeVFBykFkJmfviSZvbBbuv54ZDPGVChDXJArMAxIJZcHI6cT8UEtOEpUt8UQwtvqd1DbBw3MP5sG4fVsQao5-s6SyupjtrDGNpcg7pHnpkvbmYyHI7aDW1OZvtaph818PohDo91VOR5FJF5nqAygMfYdfNJC4rjVLowPTjuqJnxBrwoXVkhCHHDC33W-FbFIKAQJ1GbhVLTBE8UOOWxo6Dzfs9E0ng4XPo9WgJKrPkvONysSeTl_QUtyT7XbBTzWWAJhrRoWjCJRuYU486cGWSQ016vplG_zbelA8aJ0H89V6JJeoVyJPlqTzmhShyR25Zsyl1iqTnuMVOwfk522gQdMaWOSgXr0DkJs5ftiw24PPuN-XKjIPmJk8slN2JGaLETVCOQVG1AHpYuUOj1wKUUEV2ML4FSzwAHSpO4vaq7H64eKpfYGK4nqrQ_sE7PpaIQ4Ow70oAD6qow-bhtK86amp_hiUyP-qdtUvEKurprXdZwvdeB4aM7bAltP4HIaLzLw6yJugcG3zbipYJRUcqq8Aj9zNYcdjZAvNZ58oIVCbWnh6-QHs-agglwWXf7obJ5uVmhYTPxyR3ePmCOYiJG60cBRnPRQhgK3GToqAgmQFJE2LEByBGIYxlNu1uTjnkNQlOm8NPFzOR_QDVVLWkvhj7pWYUqQtSN5bS5aDE_rcqksyDuVtEi-clKoPwELaQXlv5rA10LfMWFby8Cxek6OpvWk0Dofv_eoEC2EWcO0K1EbL0EQlnje-Wj99w82IKFpsfxpUoFWbSfBKjgmePoStGt4wVnU2l1iLb-4pzW6B_lLj4DiIqgUZHaPX2SVmlC68jW-tqma-aj8RpRWJduhtzHX1zcec5UPo1axkOJ4c_897KZbcQA4="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49e6c47c081919db097750415f779","call_id":"call_0e9dc8eb2f264c4b95032558cee1ae76","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"spec\":{\"format_version\":2,\"case_id\":\"geometry-product-dimension\",\"full_target\":\"Here dimension means **Hausdorff dimension**. As approved by the user on\\n2026-10-23, assume explicitly that \\\\(E\\\\) is nonempty. With the convention\\n\\\\(\\\\dim_H\\\\varnothing=0\\\\), the printed equality would otherwise fail for\\nthe empty set. This is a disclosed addition to the printed exercise.\\n\\nLet \\\\(n\\\\geq0\\\\) be an integer, let \\\\(E\\\\subset\\\\mathbb R^n\\\\) be a nonempty\\ncompact set, and put \\\\(I=[0,1]\\\\). Identify \\\\(\\\\mathbb R^n\\\\times\\\\mathbb R\\\\)\\nwith \\\\(\\\\mathbb R^{n+1}\\\\) and use its Euclidean metric. Prove\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\dim_H(E\\\\times[0,1])=\\\\dim_H E+1.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nThe zero-dimensional ambient space \\\\(\\\\mathbb R^0\\\\) is included. A later\\nformalization using a different product norm must justify the metric change.\",\"conclusion\":\"dim_H(E × [0,1]) = dim_H E + 1, where E × [0,1] is identified with Eucl(n+1) by adjoining the last coordinate and carries the Euclidean metric. Equivalently, dim_H F = D+1.\",\"parameters\":[{\"symbol\":\"n\",\"type\":\"natural number (including zero)\"},{\"symbol\":\"E\",\"type\":\"subset of Eucl(n)\"}],\"hypotheses\":[{\"id\":\"H001\",\"statement\":\"E is nonempty.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:16-22, explicitly approved nonemptiness addition\"},{\"id\":\"H002\",\"statement\":\"E is compact in the Euclidean topology on Eucl(n).\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:21-23\"}],\"definitions\":[{\"id\":\"D001\",\"symbol\":\"Eucl\",\"type\":\"family of metric topological spaces indexed by natural numbers\",\"definition\":\"For a natural number m, Eucl(m)=R^m is the space of real coordinate vectors indexed by {0,...,m-1}; distance between x and y is (sum_{k=0}^{m-1}(x_k-y_k)^2)^(1/2). The topology is generated by open balls for this distance. In particular Eucl(0) has exactly one vector, the empty tuple. Identify Eucl(m) × R with Eucl(m+1) by (x,t)↦(x_0,...,x_{m-1},t); its distance is sqrt(dist(x,y)^2+|t-u|^2), not the maximum product distance. Compact means that every cover by open sets has a finite subcover.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"m\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"element of Eucl(m)\"},{\"symbol\":\"y\",\"type\":\"element of Eucl(m)\"},{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"u\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"m\",\"x\",\"y\",\"t\",\"u\"]},{\"id\":\"D002\",\"symbol\":\"diam\",\"type\":\"extended nonnegative real diameter of a subset of a metric space\",\"definition\":\"diam(A)=sup{dist(x,y): x,y∈A}, with diameter zero for A empty. For sets of finite diameter it is the usual nonnegative real diameter. All covers at a finite scale have finite diameters. For s>0 the cost of an empty set or a diameter-zero set is 0^s=0.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D001\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of a metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"point of that metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"y\",\"type\":\"point of that metric space\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"x\",\"y\"]},{\"id\":\"D003\",\"symbol\":\"H\",\"type\":\"scale Hausdorff contents and Hausdorff measures on Euclidean subsets, valued in [0,∞]\",\"definition\":{\"from_task\":\"problem.md\",\"start_line\":34,\"end_line\":42},\"depends_on\":[\"D001\",\"D002\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of a Euclidean space\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real exponent\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real scale\"},{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"countable family of subsets of that space\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"U\",\"diam\"]},{\"id\":\"D004\",\"symbol\":\"dim_H\",\"type\":\"Hausdorff dimension of a Euclidean subset, valued in [0,∞]\",\"definition\":\"dim_H A is inf{s∈R: s>0 and H^s(A)=0}, as an infimum in [0,∞], with infimum of the empty set infinity. In particular dim_H(empty)=0. Dimension inequalities against real numbers use their nonnegative extended-real values. Once finiteness has been proved the same symbols are also used for their real values.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D003\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of a Euclidean space\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real exponent\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"s\",\"H\"]},{\"id\":\"D005\",\"symbol\":\"I\",\"type\":\"subset of R\",\"definition\":\"I=[0,1]={t∈R:0≤t≤1}.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"t\"]},{\"id\":\"D006\",\"symbol\":\"F\",\"type\":\"subset of Eucl(n+1)\",\"definition\":\"F=E×I={(x,t):x∈E, t∈I}, using the coordinate-adjoining Euclidean identification of D001.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D001\",\"D005\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"element of Eucl(n)\"},{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"I\",\"x\",\"t\",\"Eucl\"]},{\"id\":\"D007\",\"symbol\":\"D\",\"type\":\"extended nonnegative real number\",\"definition\":\"D=dim_H E. Its finiteness and bound by n are conclusions to be proved, not conditions of this definition.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D004\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"E\"]},{\"id\":\"D008\",\"symbol\":\"λ\",\"type\":\"Lebesgue measure on R with its Borel measurable structure\",\"definition\":\"λ denotes the standard Lebesgue measure on the Borel sigma algebra of R (used also as its outer measure on arbitrary sets). For a nonnegative Borel function, ∫ g dλ denotes its extended nonnegative Lebesgue integral. Indicator notation 1_T(t) is 1 for t∈T and 0 otherwise. A sum of nonnegative terms denotes the supremum of its finite partial sums and can equal infinity.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"g\",\"type\":\"nonnegative Borel function on R\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"subset of R\"},{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"g\",\"T\",\"t\"]}],\"logic\":{\"classical\":true,\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\",\"case_elimination\",\"contradiction_classical\"]},\"pins\":{},\"inputs\":[]},\"graph\":{\"format_version\":2,\"case_id\":\"geometry-product-dimension\",\"spec_sha256\":\"controller-bound\",\"propositions\":[{\"id\":\"H001\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\"]},{\"id\":\"H002\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"Eucl\"]},{\"id\":\"E001\",\"kind\":\"external\",\"statement\":\"For a Euclidean set \\\\(A\\\\), exponent \\\\(s>0\\\\), and scale \\\\(\\\\delta>0\\\\), put\\n\\n\\\\[\\nH^s_\\\\delta(A)=\\\\inf\\\\left\\\\{\\\\sum_i(\\\\operatorname{diam}U_i)^s:\\n A\\\\subseteq\\\\bigcup_iU_i,\\\\quad\\\\operatorname{diam}U_i\\\\leq\\\\delta\\\\right\\\\},\\n\\\\qquad H^s(A)=\\\\sup_{\\\\delta>0}H^s_\\\\delta(A).\\n\\\\]\\n\\nCovers are countable, with empty members contributing zero. This\\nunnormalized Hausdorff measure gives the usual Hausdorff dimension. We use\\nits critical-exponent characterization: \\\\(H^s(A)=0\\\\) if\\n\\\\(s>\\\\dim_H A\\\\), and \\\\(H^s(A)=\\\\infty\\\\) if \\\\(0<s<\\\\dim_H A\\\\).\\nConversely, zero measure implies \\\\(\\\\dim_H A\\\\leq s\\\\), and infinite\\nmeasure implies \\\\(\\\\dim_H A\\\\geq s\\\\).\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of a finite-dimensional Euclidean space\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real exponent\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real scale\"},{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"countable covering family\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"U\",\"diam\",\"H\",\"dim_H\"],\"source\":{\"author\":\"Elias M. Stein and Rami Shakarchi (intended primary exposition); frozen proof input supplies the actual secondary statement\",\"title\":\"Real Analysis: Measure Theory, Integration, and Hilbert Spaces\",\"version\":\"Princeton Lectures in Analysis III; original edition cited in problem.md; primary text not obtained\",\"identifier\":\"10.1515/9781400835560\",\"locator\":\"Secondary statement: problem.md:34-47. Intended primary context: Chapter 7, Hausdorff measure and dimension; exact original theorem locator UNVERIFIED.\",\"notation_map\":\"The secondary H^s_δ, H^s, diam and dim_H are exactly D002-D004; covers are arbitrary countable sets, empty costs zero, positive exponents, no normalizing constant.\",\"errata\":\"Primary corrections and errata could not be inspected; no claim of an errata search succeeding.\",\"source_kind\":\"book theorem/expository basic characterization, retained solely as an explicit secondary assumption\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:34-47; not the target product theorem\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-10-30\",\"source_statement\":\"For a Euclidean set \\\\(A\\\\), exponent \\\\(s>0\\\\), and scale \\\\(\\\\delta>0\\\\), put\\n\\n\\\\[\\nH^s_\\\\delta(A)=\\\\inf\\\\left\\\\{\\\\sum_i(\\\\operatorname{diam}U_i)^s:\\n A\\\\subseteq\\\\bigcup_iU_i,\\\\quad\\\\operatorname{diam}U_i\\\\leq\\\\delta\\\\right\\\\},\\n\\\\qquad H^s(A)=\\\\sup_{\\\\delta>0}H^s_\\\\delta(A).\\n\\\\]\\n\\nCovers are countable, with empty members contributing zero. This\\nunnormalized Hausdorff measure gives the usual Hausdorff dimension. We use\\nits critical-exponent characterization: \\\\(H^s(A)=0\\\\) if\\n\\\\(s>\\\\dim_H A\\\\), and \\\\(H^s(A)=\\\\infty\\\\) if \\\\(0<s<\\\\dim_H A\\\\).\\nConversely, zero measure implies \\\\(\\\\dim_H A\\\\leq s\\\\), and infinite\\nmeasure implies \\\\(\\\\dim_H A\\\\geq s\\\\).\",\"context\":\"Complete accessible context is the frozen secondary proof's definition at problem.md:34-47. It concerns every Euclidean subset and positive exponent; it assumes neither compactness nor nonemptiness. All original primary context remains unverified.\",\"qualification\":\"UNVERIFIED_PRIMARY: conditional on this explicit secondary statement; no original-source fidelity claim.\",\"version_check\":\"2026-10-30: arxiv query unavailable; Google full-text and DOI queries unavailable; Sci-Hub lookup with the input-confirmed DOI and browser readback returned BROWSER_ERROR. Edition, original result context and correction status remain UNVERIFIED.\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a subset of a finite-dimensional Euclidean space, with the diameter-cover definition displayed in this statement.\",\"The invoked exponent is a positive real number.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"external-sources/deferred-E001.json\",\"sha256\":\"20ae7054fac2fffca329bb66a66818f37c2ac090775326723d8f952fb4d953d6\"}],\"primary_evidence\":[],\"verification\":{\"status\":\"UNVERIFIED_PRIMARY\",\"record\":{\"path\":\"external-sources/deferred-E001.json\",\"sha256\":\"20ae7054fac2fffca329bb66a66818f37c2ac090775326723d8f952fb4d953d6\"}}}},{\"id\":\"M001\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any types X and K, any measurable-space structure on X, any measure μ on X, and a countable type K, if f:K→X→[0,∞] has each f(k) almost everywhere measurable for μ, then ∫ (sum_k f(k)(x)) dμ(x) = sum_k ∫ f(k)(x) dμ(x), where integrals and sums are extended nonnegative integrals and sums.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"type with a measurable-space structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"K\",\"type\":\"countable type\"},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"measure on X\"},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"function K→X→[0,∞]\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"K\",\"μ\",\"f\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X has a measurable-space structure and μ is a measure on it.\",\"K is countable.\",\"For every k∈K, f(k) is μ-almost everywhere measurable.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M002\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any measurable space X, measure μ on X and functions f,g:X→[0,∞], if f(x)≤g(x) for every x, then ∫ f dμ≤∫ g dμ. No measurability of f or g is required.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"measurable space\"},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"measure on X\"},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"function X→[0,∞]\"},{\"symbol\":\"g\",\"type\":\"function X→[0,∞]\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"μ\",\"f\",\"g\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_mono\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is a measurable space and μ is a measure on it.\",\"For every x∈X, f(x)≤g(x).\"]}},{\"id\":\"M003\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any measurable space X, measure μ on X, measurable subset T⊆X and c∈[0,∞], the nonnegative integral of the function equal to c on T and zero off T is c·μ(T).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"measurable space\"},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"measure on X\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"extended nonnegative real\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"μ\",\"T\",\"c\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_indicator_const\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is a measurable space and μ is a measure on it.\",\"T is measurable.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M004\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any types X,K,G, a function-like type G of set functions on X with values in [0,∞] carrying an OuterMeasureClass structure, μ∈G, countable K and family T:K→Set X, one has μ(union_k T(k))≤sum_k μ(T(k)). In particular this holds for every measure or outer measure. Measurability of the sets is not required.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"type\"},{\"symbol\":\"K\",\"type\":\"countable type\"},{\"symbol\":\"G\",\"type\":\"function-like type from subsets of X to [0,∞], with OuterMeasureClass structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"element of G\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"function K→Set X\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"K\",\"G\",\"μ\",\"T\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.measure_iUnion_le\",\"hypotheses\":[\"G has FunLike and OuterMeasureClass structures on subsets of X.\",\"K is countable.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M005\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every a,b∈R, the Lebesgue measure of the closed interval [a,b] is ofReal(b-a)=max(b-a,0), interpreted as an extended nonnegative real.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Real.volume_Icc\",\"hypotheses\":[]}},{\"id\":\"M006\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every a,b∈R, the Lebesgue measure of the open interval (a,b) is ofReal(b-a)=max(b-a,0), interpreted as an extended nonnegative real.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Real.volume_Ioo\",\"hypotheses\":[]}},{\"id\":\"N001\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"E is bounded. For every s>0 and δ>0, H^s_δ(E)<∞. Moreover 0≤D≤n, so D is finite and can be regarded as a real number. If n=0, E is the singleton Eucl(0) and D=0.\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D007\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real exponent\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real scale\"}],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"H\",\"D\",\"Eucl\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:49-57 and 130-131; the finite-content assertion is exported for the slicing argument.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"dim_H F≤D+1 (in particular dim_H F is finite).\",\"definitions\":[\"D004\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"F\",\"D\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:59-92; upper product-cover construction including n=0.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"For every real s>0 and every real δ>0, H^s_δ(E)≤H^(s+1)_δ(F). All diameters and contents are for the Euclidean metrics of D001.\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D003\",\"D006\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"δ\",\"H\",\"E\",\"F\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:98-147; slicing by open interval enlargements and integration.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"If D>0 then dim_H F≥D+1.\",\"definitions\":[\"D004\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"dim_H\",\"F\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:94-149; positive-dimension lower bound.\"},{\"id\":\"N005\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"dim_H I=1 and dim_H F≥1. In particular if D=0 then dim_H F≥D+1, also when n=0.\",\"definitions\":[\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"I\",\"F\",\"D\",\"n\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:151-165; interval length estimate and nonempty vertical copy.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"kind\":\"target\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"E\",\"F\",\"D\",\"n\"]}],\"inferences\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"E001\"],\"output\":\"N001\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D007\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\",\"case_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"B\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R001/grid\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose B≥1 with E⊆[-B,B]^n, using F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R001/grid\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"In the n>0 branch let s>n be arbitrary, to be universally closed in this paragraph.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"h\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R001/grid\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Let 0<h≤1 be arbitrary in the grid estimate.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"C\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R001/grid\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set C=(2B+1)^n.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"B\",\"n\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"From H002 and the open-cover definition of compactness, the open balls of any fixed positive radius centered at all points of E have a finite subcover. For arbitrary s>0 and δ>0, apply this with radius δ/2. Every such ball has diameter at most δ by the triangle inequality, and the resulting finite δ-cover has finite s-cost, proving H^s_δ(E)<∞. Similarly a finite subcover by radius-one balls bounds E: each ball is contained in the box whose coordinate bounds are the absolute coordinates of its center plus one. The finite maximum of these coordinate bounds, increased to at least one, gives a real B≥1 with E⊆[-B,B]^n. If E has no centers the conclusion also holds with B=1, although H001 excludes that case. Thus the existence in F001 is established without presupposing boundedness.\",\"uses\":[\"H002\",\"H001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"H\",\"diam\",\"Eucl\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There exists a real B≥1 such that E⊆[-B,B]^n; also for every s>0 and δ>0, H^s_δ(E)<∞.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"B\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real\"}],\"objects\":[\"B\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"E\",\"n\",\"H\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Choose B as in F001. In the case L1: n>0, fix s>n and 0<h≤1. Divide each coordinate interval [-B,B] into ceil(2B/h) equal closed pieces, each of length at most h. Their products cover the box and hence E. The number of cubes is at most ((2B+1)/h)^n=C h^(-n), where C=(2B+1)^n, independent of h. The Euclidean diameter of each is at most sqrt(n)h, by the sum-of-squares distance formula. Their total s-cost is at most C n^(s/2)h^(s-n), which tends to zero as h decreases to zero since s-n>0. Given any target scale and any positive cost tolerance, h can be chosen small enough for both requirements. Thus H^s_δ(E)=0 for every δ>0 and H^s(E)=0. E001 then gives D≤s for every s>n; letting s decrease to n gives D≤n. This proves n>0 implies D≤n, and discharges L1. Nonnegativity follows from the nonnegative-infimum definition of dim_H.\",\"uses\":[\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"B\",\"s\",\"h\",\"C\",\"E\",\"n\",\"D\",\"H\",\"diam\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"If n>0 then 0≤D≤n.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"D\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"In the case L2: n=0, Eucl(0) consists of the empty tuple. H001 therefore gives E=Eucl(0), a singleton. Its diameter is zero, so its one-member cover has zero s-cost at every positive scale for every s>0. Thus H^s(E)=0, and E001 gives D≤s for all s>0. Since D≥0 by definition, D=0. Discharge L2 to obtain the conditional singleton and dimension assertion.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"Eucl\",\"E\",\"diam\",\"H\",\"D\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"If n=0 then E is the singleton Eucl(0) and D=0.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"E\",\"Eucl\",\"D\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[\"L2\"]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"The natural number n is either zero or positive. F002 and F003 give 0≤D≤n in both cases. F001 gives boundedness and finiteness of every positive-exponent positive-scale content. These are all the clauses of N001.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"D\",\"E\",\"H\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[{\"id\":\"A001\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"A=E, exponent s ranging over all s>n in the n>0 branch; use the zero-measure⇒dimension≤s clause.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"E⊆Eucl(n) by its parameter type; the grid costs use exactly D003.\",\"s>n>0 is the current branch range.\"]},{\"id\":\"A002\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=E⊆Eucl(0), every exponent s>0; use H^s(E)=0⇒D≤s.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"The n=0 branch and H001 identify E with the Euclidean singleton, and its zero-cost covers use D003.\",\"Each exponent in the displayed quantified argument is positive.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"inputs\":[\"N001\",\"E001\"],\"output\":\"N002\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\",\"case_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/zero\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S001\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any a>1 for the n=0 interval-cover argument.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"q\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/positive\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix a real q and temporarily assume q>D in the n≥1 branch.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\"]},{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix a real r with 0<r≤1, to be quantified in F003.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix a positive real ε, to be quantified in F003.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"countable family of nonempty subsets of Eucl(n), indexed by a countable subset of N\",\"scope\":\"R002/cover\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the positive-diameter cover U=(U_i) whose existence is F002.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"q\",\"r\",\"ε\"]},{\"symbol\":\"r_i\",\"type\":\"family of nonnegative real numbers with the same index set as U\",\"scope\":\"R002/cover\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For each index i of U define r_i=diam(U_i).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"diam\"]},{\"symbol\":\"N_i\",\"type\":\"family of positive integers indexed by the index set of U\",\"scope\":\"R002/cover\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For each index i set N_i=ceil(1/r_i).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"r_i\"]},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/scales\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any target scale δ>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"First assume L1: n=0. N001 says E is the singleton Eucl(0) and D=0. Hence the coordinate map ((),t)↦t is an isometry from F onto I. Fix any a>1. Divide I into N equal closed intervals for each positive integer N and take their inverse images in F. Their Euclidean diameters are 1/N, and total a-cost is N(1/N)^a=N^(1-a)→0 as N→∞. Consequently H^a(F)=0, and E001 gives dim_H F≤a for all a>1. It follows dim_H F≤1=D+1. Discharge L1.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"E\",\"F\",\"I\",\"D\",\"a\",\"H\",\"diam\",\"dim_H\",\"Eucl\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"If n=0 then dim_H F≤D+1.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"dim_H\",\"F\",\"D\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"For the remaining branch assume L2: n≥1. Fix q and assume L3: q>D. By N001, q>0. E001 gives H^q(E)=0. Fix r,ε and assume L4: 0<r≤1 and ε>0. Since H^q_r(E)=0, its defining infimum supplies an r-cover with q-cost below ε/2. Discard empty members. Any member of zero diameter is a singleton: two distinct points would have positive distance. Replace the singleton at index i≥0 by a ball centered at that point of diameter at most r and with q-cost less than ε·2^(-i-2). Such a positive-radius ball exists because n≥1 and q>0; take radius smaller than r/2 and (ε·2^(-i-2))^(1/q)/2. Its diameter is twice the radius (the first coordinate supplies opposite endpoints as suprema). The sum of the added costs is at most ε/2, since sum_{i≥0}2^(-i-2)=1/2. Original positive-diameter members cost less than ε/2, so the modified countable cover has total cost less than ε and all diameters in (0,r]. This proves the existence in F002.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"q\",\"D\",\"r\",\"ε\",\"E\",\"H\",\"diam\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"There exists a countable cover U=(U_i) of E by nonempty subsets of Eucl(n) such that 0<diam(U_i)≤r for every i and sum_i diam(U_i)^q<ε.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"countable family of subsets of Eucl(n)\"}],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"E\",\"n\",\"diam\",\"q\",\"r\",\"ε\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L2\",\"L3\",\"L4\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L2\",\"L3\",\"L4\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Choose U from F002, and set r_i=diam(U_i), N_i=ceil(1/r_i). Since 0<r_i≤r≤1, N_i is a positive integer, 1/N_i≤r_i and N_i≤1/r_i+1≤2/r_i. For each i partition I into N_i closed subintervals with endpoints j/N_i, 0≤j≤N_i. The sets U_i×[j/N_i,(j+1)/N_i], 0≤j<N_i, give a countable cover of F. For any two points of one such set, the first-coordinate distance is at most r_i and the last-coordinate distance at most 1/N_i≤r_i. D001 therefore bounds its Euclidean diameter by sqrt(2)r_i.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"r_i\",\"N_i\",\"r\",\"I\",\"F\",\"E\",\"n\",\"diam\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"The products U_i×[j/N_i,(j+1)/N_i], indexed by i and integers 0≤j<N_i, cover F countably and each has diameter at most sqrt(2)r_i; also N_i≤2/r_i.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"N_i\",\"r_i\",\"F\",\"diam\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L2\",\"L3\",\"L4\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"By F004 the total (q+1)-cost of this cover is at most sum_i N_i(sqrt(2)r_i)^(q+1) ≤ 2(sqrt(2))^(q+1)sum_i r_i^q < 2(sqrt(2))^(q+1)ε. Every member has diameter at most sqrt(2)r. Thus for each 0<r≤1 and ε>0 there exists a sqrt(2)r-cover of F with this cost bound. The cover's private identity is no part of the conclusion. Discharge L4 and quantify r and ε to obtain F003.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\",\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"N_i\",\"r_i\",\"q\",\"r\",\"ε\",\"F\",\"H\",\"diam\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"For every 0<r≤1 and ε>0, F has a countable cover of diameters at most sqrt(2)r and total (q+1)-cost less than 2(sqrt(2))^(q+1)ε.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"r\",\"ε\",\"F\",\"q\",\"diam\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L4\"]},{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"Fix any δ>0 and use F003 with r=min(1,δ/sqrt(2)), which is positive. The cover's diameters are at most δ. As ε ranges over arbitrarily small positive numbers, H^(q+1)_δ(F) is bounded by arbitrarily small positive costs, hence is zero. Every positive scale has zero content, so H^(q+1)(F)=0. Since q+1>0, E001 gives dim_H F≤q+1.\",\"uses\":[\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"δ\",\"q\",\"F\",\"H\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F005\",\"statement\":\"dim_H F≤q+1.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"F\",\"q\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S006\",\"text\":\"F005 holds for every q>D in the n≥1 branch. Discharge L3 and universally quantify q. N001 gives D finite, so letting q decrease to D (or taking q=D+τ for every τ>0) gives dim_H F≤D+1. Discharge L2. The alternatives n=0 and n≥1 exhaust the natural numbers; combine this branch with F001. The upper bound is finite because D≤n.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F005\"],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"D\",\"F\",\"q\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L3\",\"L2\"]}],\"applications\":[{\"id\":\"A001\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"A=F⊆Eucl(1) in the n=0 branch, exponent a>1; use zero measure⇒dimension≤a.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"F's metric is Euclidean, and the isometry is realized explicitly by interval-cover inverse images.\",\"a>1 is positive.\"]},{\"id\":\"A002\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"A=E, exponent q>D; use exponent-above-dimension⇒H^q(E)=0.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"E⊆Eucl(n) and D003 is the cover definition used.\",\"q>D≥0 by N001, so q>0.\"]},{\"id\":\"A003\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S005\",\"bindings\":\"A=F⊆Eucl(n+1), exponent q+1; use zero measure⇒dim_H F≤q+1.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"F has the Euclidean coordinate-adjoining metric and its displayed covers use D003.\",\"q>0 by S002, so q+1>0.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"inputs\":[\"N001\",\"M001\",\"M002\",\"M003\",\"M005\",\"M006\"],\"output\":\"N003\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D008\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix a real exponent s; assume s>0 together with δ>0 under L1.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix a real scale δ; its positivity belongs to L1.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"V\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of Eucl(n+1)\",\"scope\":\"R003/covers\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any countable covering family V=(V_i), padded with empty sets if finite, under L2 that it covers F and every diameter is at most δ.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"F\",\"δ\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ρ\",\"type\":\"sequence of nonnegative real numbers\",\"scope\":\"R003/covers\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set ρ_i=diam(V_i), with ρ_i=0 for empty V_i.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"diam\"]},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of Eucl(n)\",\"scope\":\"R003/covers\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set A_i={x: there is t with (x,t)∈V_i}, the first-coordinate projection.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"B\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of R\",\"scope\":\"R003/covers\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set B_i={t: there is x with (x,t)∈V_i}, the last-coordinate projection.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/enlargement\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix a real ε and assume ε>0 under L3.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"η\",\"type\":\"sequence of positive real numbers\",\"scope\":\"R003/enlargement\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define η_i=ε·2^(-i-1)/(1+ρ_i^s).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"ε\",\"ρ\",\"s\"]},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"finite nonnegative real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define c=H^s_δ(E); N001 gives finiteness under L1.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"H\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"E\"]},{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"sequence of Borel subsets of R, each empty or a bounded open interval\",\"scope\":\"R003/integration\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the family J=(J_i) supplied by F001, enclosing every B_i.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"B\",\"ρ\",\"η\"]},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"function R→[0,∞]\",\"scope\":\"R003/integration\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set f(t)=c·1_I(t).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"I\"]},{\"symbol\":\"g\",\"type\":\"sequence of functions R→[0,∞]\",\"scope\":\"R003/integration\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set g_i(t)=ρ_i^s·1_(J_i∩I)(t).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"ρ\",\"s\",\"J\",\"I\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Fix real s,δ and assume L1: s>0, δ>0. Put c=H^s_δ(E), finite by N001. Fix an arbitrary sequence V and assume L2: it is a δ-cover of F; finite countable covers can be padded by empty sets. Define ρ_i=diam(V_i), A_i and B_i as its first and last coordinate projections. The Euclidean distance formula gives coordinate distances at most the full distance, hence diam(A_i),diam(B_i)≤ρ_i≤δ. Fix ε and assume L3: ε>0. Define η_i=ε·2^(-i-1)/(1+ρ_i^s)>0. For nonempty V_i, B_i is nonempty and bounded (choose one of its points; every other is within δ). Its real infimum and supremum exist and sup B_i-inf B_i≤ρ_i by the diameter bound. The open interval (inf B_i-η_i/2, sup B_i+η_i/2) contains B_i and has length ≤ρ_i+η_i. For empty V_i use the empty set instead. Thus the sequence of open enclosing intervals required in F001 exists. No measurability of V_i,A_i or B_i is asserted or needed.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"δ\",\"c\",\"H\",\"E\",\"V\",\"ρ\",\"A\",\"B\",\"ε\",\"η\",\"F\",\"diam\",\"n\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There exists a sequence J such that if V_i is nonempty then J_i is a bounded open interval containing B_i with length at most ρ_i+η_i, and if V_i is empty then J_i is empty.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of R\"}],\"objects\":[\"J\",\"V\",\"B\",\"ρ\",\"η\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Choose J from F001. For arbitrary t∈I and x∈E, (x,t)∈F, so some V_i contains (x,t). Then x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i. Hence the A_i with t∈J_i cover E. They have diameter at most ρ_i≤δ; pad the remaining indices by empty sets. The definition of c as an infimum of cover costs gives c≤sum_i diam(A_i)^s 1_(J_i)(t)≤sum_i ρ_i^s 1_(J_i)(t). This proves F002 pointwise for all t∈I.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"J\",\"V\",\"A\",\"B\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"c\",\"E\",\"F\",\"I\",\"diam\",\"H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"For every t∈I, c≤sum_{i≥0} ρ_i^s 1_(J_i)(t).\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"t\",\"I\",\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"J\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"On all of R define f(t)=c·1_I(t) and g_i(t)=ρ_i^s·1_(J_i∩I)(t). F002 gives f≤sum_i g_i, including outside I where both sides vanish. Each J_i is open or empty and I is closed, so J_i∩I is Borel; the nonnegative constant indicators g_i are measurable and hence λ-almost everywhere measurable. Apply M002 to this pointwise inequality and M001 to the measurable nonnegative series. M003 evaluates the constant indicators, and M005 gives λ(I)=1. Thus c=cλ(I)=∫f dλ≤∫sum_i g_i dλ=sum_i∫g_i dλ=sum_i ρ_i^s λ(J_i∩I). By measure monotonicity and M006, λ(J_i∩I)≤λ(J_i)≤ρ_i+η_i (empty intervals have measure zero). It follows that c≤sum_i ρ_i^s(ρ_i+η_i)≤sum_i ρ_i^(s+1)+sum_i η_iρ_i^s≤sum_i ρ_i^(s+1)+ε, since η_iρ_i^s≤ε·2^(-i-1) and sum_{i≥0}2^(-i-1)=1. These inequalities of nonnegative series follow first for finite partial sums and then by their suprema. They include ρ_i=0 because s>0. No interchange of signed or nonmeasurable functions has occurred.\",\"uses\":[\"M001\",\"M002\",\"M003\",\"M005\",\"M006\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"f\",\"g\",\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"η\",\"ε\",\"J\",\"I\",\"λ\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"c≤sum_i ρ_i^(s+1)+ε.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"ε\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"The bound F003 holds for every ε>0, with c and the original V,ρ fixed independently of ε. Discharge L3 and quantify ε. If sum_i ρ_i^(s+1)=∞ then c≤this sum immediately. If it is finite, any strict inequality c>sum_i ρ_i^(s+1) would be contradicted by choosing ε smaller than their positive difference. Thus c≤sum_i ρ_i^(s+1) in all cases. Discharge L2 and quantify V: every δ-cover of F has (s+1)-cost at least c.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"ε\",\"V\",\"δ\",\"F\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"Every countable δ-cover of F has total (s+1)-cost at least c=H^s_δ(E).\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"δ\",\"F\",\"s\",\"c\",\"H\",\"E\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L3\",\"L2\"]},{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"Taking the infimum of the costs in F004 gives H^s_δ(E)≤H^(s+1)_δ(F). Discharge L1 and universally quantify the real s,δ, retaining their positive-range conditions. This proves N003 at every positive scale.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"H\",\"E\",\"F\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"c\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"X=R with Borel measurable structure, μ=λ, K=N, source f(i)=g_i=ρ_i^s 1_(J_i∩I).\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"λ is Lebesgue measure on the Borel space R by D008.\",\"The index type N is countable.\",\"J_i∩I is Borel since J_i is open or empty by F001 and I is closed; constant indicator functions on these sets are measurable, hence almost everywhere measurable.\"]},{\"input\":\"M002\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"X=R, μ=λ, source f=c 1_I and source g=sum_i g_i.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"The Borel space R and its measure λ are D008.\",\"F002 gives the inequality on I; off I the indicators on both sides vanish.\"]},{\"id\":\"A101\",\"input\":\"M003\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"X=R, μ=λ, T=I, constant=c, and also for every i, T=J_i∩I and constant=ρ_i^s.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"D008 supplies the measurable space and λ.\",\"I is closed and therefore Borel; each J_i is open or empty by F001, so J_i∩I is Borel.\"]},{\"input\":\"M005\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"a=0,b=1; λ(I)=ofReal(1-0)=1.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]},{\"input\":\"M006\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"For each nonempty J_i take a=inf B_i-η_i/2, b=sup B_i+η_i/2 from F001's construction; the same length bound is part of F001 even for another enclosing witness.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]}]},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"inputs\":[\"N001\",\"N003\",\"E001\"],\"output\":\"N004\",\"definitions\":[\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R004/positive\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Under D>0 fix any real s and assume 0<s<D.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Assume L1: D>0. Fix s and assume L2: 0<s<D. E001 gives H^s(E)=∞. N003 gives H^s_δ(E)≤H^(s+1)_δ(F) for every δ>0. Taking suprema over positive δ yields ∞=H^s(E)≤H^(s+1)(F), so the latter is infinite. Equivalently, for every finite bound there is a scale with the left content above that bound, and all smaller scales have at least as large a content, because shrinking the admissible cover class can only increase an infimum. This explicitly justifies the small-scale limiting assertion of the supplied proof. E001 with exponent s+1 gives dim_H F≥s+1. Discharge L2 and quantify s in its range.\",\"uses\":[\"N003\",\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"s\",\"H\",\"E\",\"F\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"For every real s with 0<s<D, dim_H F≥s+1.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"D\",\"dim_H\",\"F\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[\"L2\"]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"N001 gives 0<D≤n in the present branch, so D is a finite real number. The supremum of s+1 over 0<s<D is D+1: choose s arbitrarily close to D from below, for example s=D-D/k for integers k>1. F001 therefore gives dim_H F≥D+1. Discharge L1 to obtain precisely N004.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"n\",\"s\",\"F\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]}],\"applications\":[{\"id\":\"A001\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"A=E, exponent s with 0<s<D=dim_H E; use the infinite-measure-below-dimension clause.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"E⊆Eucl(n) and H is D003.\",\"L2 states 0<s<D, in particular s>0.\"]},{\"id\":\"A002\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"A=F⊆Eucl(n+1), exponent s+1; use infinite measure⇒dimension≥s+1.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"F is the Euclidean subset D006 and its measure is D003.\",\"s>0 by L2, so s+1>0.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"M004\",\"M005\",\"M006\",\"E001\"],\"output\":\"N005\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\",\"D008\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R005/upper\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S001\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Let any a>1 be fixed for the interval upper bound.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R005/lower\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix real s under the assumption 0<s<1, later universally closed.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R005/lower\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix real δ under the assumption δ>0, later quantified.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"W\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of R\",\"scope\":\"R005/covers\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any sequence W under the assumption it is a δ-cover of I.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"δ\",\"I\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ρ\",\"type\":\"sequence of nonnegative real numbers\",\"scope\":\"R005/covers\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set ρ_i=diam(W_i).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"diam\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R005/covers\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary ε under ε>0 for open enlargements.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"sequence of open intervals or empty sets in R\",\"scope\":\"R005/covers\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the enclosing intervals J_i with the properties proved in F002.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"ρ\",\"ε\"]},{\"symbol\":\"x0\",\"type\":\"element of Eucl(n)\",\"scope\":\"R005/embedding\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose x0∈E using H001, the existence of a point of E.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"For every a>1, dividing I into N equal closed pieces gives diameters 1/N and total a-cost N^(1-a)→0 as positive integers N→∞. These become arbitrarily fine covers with arbitrarily small cost, so H^a(I)=0. E001 implies dim_H I≤a for every a>1, hence dim_H I≤1.\",\"uses\":[\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"a\",\"I\",\"H\",\"diam\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"dim_H I≤1.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"I\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Fix s,δ and assume L1: 0<s<1 and δ>0. Fix W and assume L2: W is a countable δ-cover of I, padded by empty sets if necessary. Put ρ_i=diam(W_i)≤δ. Fix ε and assume L3: ε>0. For each nonempty W_i, its real infimum and supremum exist, and sup W_i-inf W_i≤ρ_i. Enlarge to the open interval (inf W_i-ε·2^(-i-2),sup W_i+ε·2^(-i-2)), of length at most ρ_i+ε·2^(-i-1). Empty members need no enlargement. This constructs the intervals whose existence is F002.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"δ\",\"W\",\"ρ\",\"I\",\"ε\",\"diam\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"There is a sequence J of open intervals or empty sets with W_i⊆J_i and length(J_i)≤ρ_i+ε·2^(-i-1) for every i; J_i is empty when W_i is empty.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of R\"}],\"objects\":[\"J\",\"W\",\"ρ\",\"ε\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Choose J as in F002. Since I⊆union_i J_i, measure monotonicity, M005, M004 and M006 give 1=λ(I)≤λ(union_i J_i)≤sum_i λ(J_i)≤sum_i ρ_i+ε·sum_i 2^(-i-1)=sum_i ρ_i+ε. Subadditivity applies to the countable family without any assumption on the original W_i; only the enclosing intervals are measured. Discharge L3 and use arbitrariness of ε>0. If sum_i ρ_i is infinite the conclusion is immediate; otherwise a positive difference argument yields sum_i ρ_i≥1. For ρ_i>0, since 0<ρ_i≤δ and s-1<0, ρ_i^s=ρ_i·ρ_i^(s-1)≥δ^(s-1)ρ_i. The same inequality is true when ρ_i=0 because both sides are zero. Taking partial sums and then their suprema gives sum_i ρ_i^s≥δ^(s-1)sum_i ρ_i≥δ^(s-1). Discharge L2 and universally quantify W.\",\"uses\":[\"M004\",\"M005\",\"M006\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"J\",\"W\",\"ρ\",\"ε\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"I\",\"λ\",\"diam\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"Every countable δ-cover of I has s-cost at least δ^(s-1).\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"δ\",\"I\",\"s\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L3\",\"L2\"]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"Taking the infimum in F003 gives H^s_δ(I)≥δ^(s-1). As δ decreases to zero this tends to infinity since 0<s<1. Thus H^s(I)=∞. E001 gives dim_H I≥s for every 0<s<1. Quantifying δ and then s and letting s increase to one yields dim_H I≥1, and F001 gives equality. Discharge L1, obtaining F004 with the whole quantified measure assertion included for later use.\",\"uses\":[\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"δ\",\"H\",\"I\",\"dim_H\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"dim_H I=1 and for every real s with 0<s<1, H^s(I)=∞.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"I\",\"s\",\"H\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]},{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"Choose x0∈E from H001. The map t↦(x0,t) from I into F preserves distances, because sqrt(dist(x0,x0)^2+|t-u|^2)=|t-u|. Here is the cover-based monotonicity argument for this particular isometric embedding, so no separate dimension theorem is tacitly invoked: given any positive scale δ and any countable δ-cover V_i of F, the sets {t∈I:(x0,t)∈V_i} cover I and have diameter at most diam(V_i). Thus for every exponent s>0, H^s_δ(I)≤H^s_δ(F), and taking suprema over δ>0 gives H^s(I)≤H^s(F). By F004, H^s(F)=∞ for all 0<s<1. E001 gives dim_H F≥s for every such s, hence dim_H F≥1. Combined with F004 this proves the two dimension assertions in N005. If D=0, this lower bound reads dim_H F≥D+1. The construction of the vertical copy works unchanged for the unique point of Eucl(0); no positive ambient dimension was used.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"E001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"x0\",\"E\",\"n\",\"I\",\"F\",\"s\",\"H\",\"diam\",\"dim_H\",\"D\",\"Eucl\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[{\"id\":\"A001\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"A=I⊆R, exponent a>1; apply zero measure⇒dimension≤a.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"I is the Euclidean interval D005 and its covers use D003.\",\"a>1 implies a>0.\"]},{\"input\":\"M004\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"X=R, G=the type of measures on the Borel space R, μ=λ, K=N, T(i)=J_i.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"The measure λ has the function-like set evaluation and OuterMeasureClass structures of a measure.\",\"N is countable.\"]},{\"input\":\"M005\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"a=0,b=1, giving λ(I)=1.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]},{\"input\":\"M006\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"For each nonempty J_i use its real left and right endpoints; their difference is its length, bounded in F002.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]},{\"id\":\"A002\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"A=I⊆R, exponent s∈(0,1); apply infinite measure⇒dimension≥s.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"I is a subset of the Euclidean line and the measure is D003.\",\"0<s<1 is L1.\"]},{\"id\":\"A003\",\"input\":\"E001\",\"at\":\"S005\",\"bindings\":\"A=F⊆Eucl(n+1), for every exponent s∈(0,1); apply infinite measure⇒dimension≥s.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"D006 gives the Euclidean subset, and the pullback argument uses exactly D003, with no metric change.\",\"Every exponent in this quantified application satisfies 0<s<1.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"inputs\":[\"N001\",\"N002\",\"N004\",\"N005\"],\"output\":\"P\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"case_elimination\"],\"locals\":[],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"By N001, D is a finite nonnegative real number. If D>0, N004 gives dim_H F≥D+1. If D=0, N005 gives dim_H F≥1=D+1; these alternatives exhaust D≥0. N002 gives dim_H F≤D+1 in every ambient dimension, including n=0. The two inequalities yield dim_H F=D+1. Substituting F=E×[0,1] and D=dim_H E is exactly the claimed equality, with the coordinate-adjoining Euclidean identification fixed in D001 and no norm replacement.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"N002\",\"N004\",\"N005\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"F\",\"E\",\"I\",\"n\",\"dim_H\",\"Eucl\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[]}]}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidate","readiness","open_issues","original_context_note","output_notes","inference_notes"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"83a7df5c-2374-4dcf-b6b5-a4649a1eebd9","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"high"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51987,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":15467,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1034},"total_tokens":67454,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d1a66e88191b648504d36816c9d":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d1d46c0819196e1236b0001585a":{"input_tokens":30,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d20d4148191aa34bfc3a8314e32":{"input_tokens":27,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d242c40819190765a8b4a799af0":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d284dfc819194c272525c1116d9":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d2dc184819181d3a62b1000a1af":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d33da488191b2918857681c9575":{"input_tokens":38,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d378dcc819185de1b4b95f2138e":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d3f235081919a06adf86dc7105f":{"input_tokens":35,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d44164481918c13ac7f52d6c66a":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfedefea67727b6016ae49d88f2788191be362c5fcad1700f":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_